:: Morning After 5 [event main_quest] {"position":"6825,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Morning After", last part: that night in my room. Applies the effects and finishes the quest; its set
   (Define Quests) takes every device but the original off the books, the vent unit too, takes $ethan.name off the staff
   and his projects, and sets his 2 percent back to 0. Then Morning After End, the title card. $company.stage stays 1:
   Stage 2 is not built yet (a new office, Suspicion), so the game keeps running in the Stage 1 office until it is. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[1].img>><</silent>>
Later, in my room, I put the original on the nightstand where I built it, between the blinking clock and a notebook full of sketches I drew before any of this was real.

Yesterday I had a server full of data nobody else in the world has, a shelf of products, a unit in the ceiling that made people love coming to work, and a best friend who wrote most of my code. Tonight I have this one, a hardware guy who never throws anything away, a lawyer over a dry cleaner's, a report with $sister.callName's smile on the cover, and a case number I'm supposed to keep somewhere safe. And I have them.

Through the wall I can hear the house settling for the night, the pipes, the stairs, the kind of quiet that only happens when everyone's home. Down the hall, <<if $flags.supplierOffered === true>>$sister.callName's door is open and her bed is empty, and from $mom.callName's room there's the murmur of two voices, too low to make out, and then nothing<<else>>$mom.callName is humming something while she gets ready for bed, and $sister.callName is laughing at something on her phone, a little too loud, so that I'll hear it<</if>>.

$ethan.name walked out with almost everything I built, and he was probably right about most of it. But he took the part I can build again. The device was only ever how I got them here, and they're still here, exactly where I put them, and tomorrow, when I ask, they'll tell me anything I want to know.

<<Media "images/events/morning_after/nightstand.jpg" 600>>
/* A small device on a cluttered nightstand next to a blinking digital clock, in a dark bedroom */

<<UpdateStat "-" "Morale" 10>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "Reputation" 10>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 3>>
<<Feel $mom "ethan" -2 "lasting">>
<<Feel $sister "ethan" -2 "lasting">>
<<if $flags.supplierOffered === true>>
<<ProfileLog $mom "The Morning After" "The night of the club, $ethan.name walked out with almost everything the company owned. She made soup, kept a hand on $sister.callName's back all through dinner, and offered to tell me about the night before, whenever I ask.">>
<<ProfileLog $sister "The Morning After" "The night of the club, $ethan.name walked out with almost everything the company owned. She didn't ask what he took. She sat across from me in $mom.callName's old cardigan with her foot against mine, and let me know she'd tell me about the club too, if I ask.">>
<<else>>
<<ProfileLog $mom "The Morning After" "$ethan.name walked out in the night with almost everything the company owned. She made me sit down and fed me before she asked a single question.">>
<<ProfileLog $sister "The Morning After" "$ethan.name walked out in the night with almost everything the company owned. She stole my bread until I laughed, and told me I'd build the next one out of something else.">>
<</if>>
<<ProfileMemory $mom "The empty desk" "$ethan.name used to eat everything in our fridge when he was sixteen. She always liked him, and the day he left she cooked for the rest of us anyway and didn't say his name once.">>
<<NextQuest $player>>

